entityDescription:
The National Center for Cartography, in carrying out its object of activity, fulfills the following attributions:
a) ensures the modernization of the geodetic and leveling networks at national level, as well as the participation with data in order to ensure the maintenance of the national system of permanent GNSS stations;
b) performs geodetic, topographic and gravimetric works for the maintenance and modernization of the support, thickening, lifting and quasi-geoid networks at national level;
c) creates and updates the official map of Romania in analog and digital format, as well as the digital model of the terrain, including the use of data provided free of charge by other institutions and competent authorities, as the case may be;
d) participates with data and information in the realization and maintenance of the spatial data infrastructure at national level for the transposition of the INSPIRE Directive in Romania;
e) processes photogrammetric and remote sensing recordings;
f) participates in the creation and administration of the national geodetic and cartographic database, together with the territorial offices;
g) provides and realizes, upon request, specialized works and products derived from the existing data in its own databases and in those existing in the archive of the National Agency and of the territorial offices;
h) participates in the recovery of the data obtained from the reception of the specialized technical works and their integration in the national geodetic and cartographic database;
i) participates in the realization and updating of methodologies, technical specifications, norms, technological standards, models and geodetic and cartographic data structures;
j) ensures the technical support and the participation in the development and reception of the specialized works realized within the National Program of cadastre and land book;
k) organizes research and development in specific fields of activity;
l) creates and develops specialized systems and technologies based on existing data;
m) issues the approval for the beginning of the works and realizes the reception for the works of geodesy, cartography, photogrammetry, remote sensing and aerofocography;
n) ensures the printing of the analog and digital support for the realization of the information and public awareness campaign of the citizens;
o) participates in the implementation of domestic and international projects in which the National Agency is involved;
p) executes, upon request, specialized works in the field of activity, for a fee based on the Time Norms approved by the National Agency.
q) maintains and administers the Romanian Position Determination System (ROMPOS).

